+### 7.6 pi-durable: the snapshot is the copy, the row is the unit
+
+`pi-durable` (third session source, GLG ruling 2026-10-06) stores sessions in a
+live SQLite DB, not an append-only text file. Every corpus rule that the JSONL
+sources got for free from the file format has to be restated for rows.
+
+1. **A live DB is never copied, only snapshotted.** Committed rows of a live
+   durable session sit in the WAL; the main file alone can have no tables at all
+   (measured 2026-10-06: 4,096-byte main file, 3.8 MB WAL, `no such table:
+   entries` on the copy and under `immutable=1`; complete under `VACUUM INTO` and
+   the backup API). The snapshot is taken by `VACUUM INTO` from a read-only
+   connection on the host that owns the DB, and is the only thing that travels.
+2. **The snapshot is made where the DB lives.** The index authority does not
+   reach a remote durable DB through rsync. A peer's snapshot is produced on the
+   peer (piped stdlib script, as `corpus-admit.py` already is) and carried as a
+   closed file.
+3. **Append-only moves from the file to the row.** A newer snapshot replaces the
+   corpus copy only if it holds every entry id the old copy held, passes
+   `quick_check`, and has a supported schema. A shrinking or unreadable snapshot
+   never overwrites memory; the gather keeps the old copy and says so.
+4. **The durable runtime is not ours.** No native code, lock, migration or
+   `Harness.open` path is used to read; nothing is added to the runtime to make
+   it readable. A schema version above the supported one is refused by name.
+5. **Classify by kind and submission, never by role.** `pi.compaction` and
+   handoff `pi.reset` carry `role: "user"`. A role-based reader indexes summaries
+   and handoffs as GLG's words — the exact corruption this axis exists to avoid.
+6. **Physical rows only.** Fork history is inherited by scan, not stored twice;
+   any reader that walks per-conversation history must de-duplicate by entry id.
+7. **The watermark follows the flush.** A file's embedded-entry watermark is
+   persisted only after the WriteBuffer has flushed every chunk below it — 6.4 /
+   6.5, restated for a cursor instead of an mtime.
+
+`dedupeByBasename` is unsafe for this source: every durable session is named
+`session.sqlite`. Identity is the session directory.
+
